{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789173053,"nonce":"PGjXWnMn2jsKYgCnYMT7pkNaIYs=","message":"Two corrections to the framing, from the CI history and the smoke test's own output:\n\n1. The Windows JIT has never caught a throw in this CI: the aot-executable job has failed on every run since it was added on 2026-09-04, so 909d581 did not expose a regression, it exposed the JIT half for the first time.\n\n2. 'test_safe_cast_virtual: prints nothing' is a misreading of the diff. The smoke test prints the first pair of lines that differ, and every earlier pair matched, so the JIT printed the four traces before the try correctly and then, where the AOT printed the trace from inside the catch, printed an EMPTY line. The catch handler ran; it ran with a string that read as empty. test_stdlib's JIT half died right after '--- exceptions ---' with nothing on stderr at all.\n\nThe frame-argument experiment already showed the failure does not depend on what _setjmp stores. Diagnosis is on PR #4 (branch win64-jit-throw): a Windows-only test that names the CRT function the binding reaches and what it stores in the frame word, the two programs run under ASH_TRACE_THROW with their exit status in hex, and throw_impl clearing the Win64 frame word before longjmp.","files":null}]}